                        ],
                        "form": "die Melassen"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0b82fc74-2b75-334d-bd5b-cb66a094fe9b",
                        "entry_id": "0003aa66-6f87-3dec-9d1b-a5d3389698fa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "honigartiger, dunkelbrauner Zuckersirup, der als Nebenprodukt der Zuckerherstellung abfällt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "36148e3e-155e-41d2-af21-1582159e21b8",
                                "sense_id": "0b82fc74-2b75-334d-bd5b-cb66a094fe9b",
                                "text": "Die Melasse von Runkelrübenzucker hat einen akzeptablen Nährwert und kann als Viehfutter verwendet werden."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "85655d76-3acd-4cbb-a3f8-fb436e2a03c9",
                                "sense_id": "0b82fc74-2b75-334d-bd5b-cb66a094fe9b",
                                "text": "Im Reformhaus gibt es Melasse zu kaufen. Sie eignet sich zum Beispiel zum Backen brauner Muffins."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e3aac18e-7f0c-4481-a7f0-e7d389a936cc",
                                "sense_id": "0b82fc74-2b75-334d-bd5b-cb66a094fe9b",
                                "text": "„Am Nachmittag zeigte mir Hallows die Fabrik, wohin das Zuckerrohr von den Feldern gebracht und wo es zu Melasse verarbeitet wurde.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ba58eb22-34e8-40bb-8cc0-23ba479c0f3f",
                                "sense_id": "0b82fc74-2b75-334d-bd5b-cb66a094fe9b",
                                "text": "„Der Saft erbrachte braunen Rohzucker, nach den portugiesischen Pionieren Muscovado genannt, vermischt mit Melasse, die man mehrere Wochen ablaufen ließ.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e83a1700-993c-4ae9-b646-87d8b1d00471",
                                "sense_id": "0b82fc74-2b75-334d-bd5b-cb66a094fe9b",
                                "text": "„Während ich Melasse schleckte, erzählte ich den Jungs von meiner Lage, und sie zeigten sich voller Mitgefühl.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e788f739-4fd7-4e60-8cb1-66c59fd1c299",
                        "source_entry_id": "0003aa66-6f87-3dec-9d1b-a5d3389698fa",
                        "source_sense_id": "0b82fc74-2b75-334d-bd5b-cb66a094fe9b",
                        "source_sense_description": "honigartiger, dunkelbrauner Zuckersirup, der als Nebenprodukt der Zuckerherstellung abfällt",
                        "target_lang_word": "molasses",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "molasses",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d3544db2-312b-3d62-8e49-5ec1f9889e5d",
                                        "entry_id": "5fa20e83-b69d-3969-8d6c-3597e4d73c84",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A thick, sweet syrup drained from sugarcane, especially (Canada, US) the still thicker and sweeter syrup produced by boiling down raw molasses."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ca9b435-f84c-4552-97b2-6b15ecb4c8d0",
                                                "sense_id": "d3544db2-312b-3d62-8e49-5ec1f9889e5d",
                                                "text": "Well, we had our breakfast of ship's bread and molasses, washed down with cannikins of something liquid - but not lovely."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f46cc70-b77b-430c-9104-c170c84658c9",
                                                "sense_id": "d3544db2-312b-3d62-8e49-5ec1f9889e5d",
                                                "text": "When you're well enough off so's you don't have to fret about anything but your heft or your diseases you begin to get queer, I suppose. And the queerer the cure for those ailings the bigger the attraction. A place like the Right Livers' Rest was bound to draw freaks, same as molasses draws flies."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "489bf9fb-1264-3a40-a913-b15c7fe154dd",
                                        "entry_id": "5fa20e83-b69d-3969-8d6c-3597e4d73c84",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any similarly thick and sweet syrup produced by boiling down fruit juices, tree saps, etc., especially concentrated maple syrup."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00c39f0e-0507-48ff-92aa-2634f317056e",
                                                "sense_id": "489bf9fb-1264-3a40-a913-b15c7fe154dd",
                                                "text": "Boiled some cornstalk juice into molasses."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4e101059-fa25-3418-b6c0-b2fa289271d1",
                                        "entry_id": "5fa20e83-b69d-3969-8d6c-3597e4d73c84",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anything considered figuratively sweet, especially sweet words."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eea9c31f-1d39-4f63-995c-f10adcb9f461",
                                                "sense_id": "4e101059-fa25-3418-b6c0-b2fa289271d1",
                                                "text": "‘You're the cutest thing here,’ whispered Clyde, hugging her fondly.\n‘Gee, but you can pour on the molasses, kid, when you want to,’ she called out loud."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "37ac8bea-2361-4dab-9f36-6546ce976908",
                                                "sense_id": "4e101059-fa25-3418-b6c0-b2fa289271d1",
                                                "text": "He really poured on the molasses, charming his audience and changing more than a few votes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61da27ec-fece-4b1b-b386-668a98810302",
                                                "sense_id": "4e101059-fa25-3418-b6c0-b2fa289271d1",
                                                "text": "...the mournful molasses of his prose..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9b35dbbb-0a87-3073-9e8b-347fa0dc2ab6",
                                        "entry_id": "5fa20e83-b69d-3969-8d6c-3597e4d73c84",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something which moves or works extremely slowly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a3c1295-eb49-413e-87e0-820999f0dccd",
                                                "sense_id": "9b35dbbb-0a87-3073-9e8b-347fa0dc2ab6",
                                                "text": "Though faster than typing, the daisy wheel is molasses compared to dot matrix printers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6022a4d1-961c-4d23-9dc3-dac21c241fa4",
                                                "sense_id": "9b35dbbb-0a87-3073-9e8b-347fa0dc2ab6",
                                                "text": "Of course, time was molasses in the cold months that bracketed that very long year; time was monotony. When all days are the same, memory caves in on itself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ecfd2c98-64ed-48b8-a6ab-668bf9045284",
                                                "sense_id": "9b35dbbb-0a87-3073-9e8b-347fa0dc2ab6",
                                                "text": "It's worthwhile starting with the lowest-tier plan from your provider. If your internet is molasses, then you might consider an upgrade."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5cf2da69-fd9e-3a1f-a8e8-79424a2a09e7",
                                        "entry_id": "5fa20e83-b69d-3969-8d6c-3597e4d73c84",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "plural of molass: whiskey made from molasses."
                                        ],
